<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · infrastructure</p><h1 class="enc-title">Keban Dam</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1974</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Keban Dam is a hydroelectric dam on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euphrates">Euphrates</a> in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>, completed in 1974 near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elazig">Elazığ</a>. It was the first of the large dams on the upper Euphrates and created one of Turkey's largest <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reservoir">reservoirs</a>. Before the flooding, an international rescue excavation project investigated many ancient settlement mounds in the Elazığ plain.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/keban-dam.jpg" alt="Keban Dam" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Heinz it up 57 at en.wikipedia · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:KebanDam.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
